      "id": "l01",
      "start": 0.45,
      "end": 3.821,
      "text": "The dot is right, so why is the arrow wrong next to a speaker?",
      "words": 14,
      "words_per_s": 4.15,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 14.7
    },
    {
      "id": "l02",
      "start": 4.35,
      "end": 11.108,
      "text": "GPS places the dot. The arrow comes from a tiny compass sensor that feels Earth's magnetic field.",
      "words": 17,
      "words_per_s": 2.52,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.7
    },
    {
      "id": "l03",
      "start": 11.55,
      "end": 17.575,
      "text": "That field is weak. Up close, a speaker's magnet or a steel desk can bend it, and the arrow swings.",
      "words": 20,
      "words_per_s": 3.32,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 15.1
    },
    {
      "id": "l04",
      "start": 18.65,
      "end": 23.155,
      "text": "Step away from magnets and steel, then calibrate by waving a figure eight.",
      "words": 13,
      "words_per_s": 2.89,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.5
    },
    {
      "id": "l05",
      "start": 26.35,
      "end": 29.639,
      "text": "Download Recall for learning any new subject with AI.",
      "words": 9,
      "words_per_s": 2.74,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 15.5
    }
  ],
